course: dictionary
lesson: 10011
title: Temperature: how hot or cold
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Temperature tells you how hot or cold something is. Scientists measure it in degrees with a thermometer. «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection» shows that the temperature of a body can go up when you are ill.
explain: Your body temperature is how warm your body is. Normal is about 37 degrees Celsius, so «normal body temperature is about 36.5 to 37.5 degrees Celsius» is the usual range. When someone says they have a temperature, they mean they have a fever.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Chocolate melts just below body temperature, so it melts in your pocket and in your mouth but stays hard on a cool shelf.» Pocket, mouth and shelf tell you that temperature here is about how warm or cool something is. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Temperature tells how hot or cold something is.
fact: We measure temperature in degrees with a thermometer.
fact: Water freezes at 0 °C and boils at 100 °C.
fact: «Gritters spread salt before a frost because salty water freezes at a lower temperature than plain water.»
fact: To have a temperature means to have a fever.
exercise: What does temperature tell you? | How big something is | How heavy something is | How long something lasts | *How hot or cold something is
exercise: «Chocolate melts just below body temperature.» What is body temperature here? | The weight of your body | How fast you run | The number of bones you have | *How warm your body is
exercise: Water freezes at 0 °C. Is 0 degrees hotter or colder than 10 degrees? | *Colder | Hotter | Neither | The same
test: Nina has a temperature and stays in bed. What does having a temperature mean? | Feeling very tired after a long walk | Being very happy | *Having a fever | Feeling hungry
test: «Salty water freezes at a lower temperature than plain water.» Which water freezes at a lower temperature? | Both freeze at 100 °C | *Salty water | Plain water | Neither freezes
exam: Which word means how hot or cold something is? | Thermometer | Fever | *Temperature | Degrees
